2026-10-10T04:49:17Z  NOTE      fix: handleMarkReadReply accepts any 2xx without parsing. The JSON-object requirement (fromJson + isObject) was the only path from a 2xx to failure, and 204 No Content carries an empty body — so the server accepted mark-all-read while the client reported "Mark all read returned invalid JSON" and kept every notification unread. The bounded-body read is retained (a policy breach is still a failure even on 2xx); only the shape requirement is gone, mirroring SunoLibraryMutations::handleReply which the board cites as getting this right. Per the inventory rule: a 2xx on a mutation route means accepted, shape unverified — parse nothing.
2026-10-10T04:49:17Z  NOTE      tests: the suite is pure-function only (its own main, no reply harness; constructing a SunoClient would touch the keychain), and the deleted block was the entire defect — the regression story is structural: with the block gone, no path from 2xx to failure remains. The request-shape contract stays pinned by the existing parsesBadgeAndMarkAllReadContract test.
